data/rcap-all50/overlays/census-v1/hi/rcap-hi-custom-pleading--custom-pleading/participant-instructions.md:296:4. File the motion in your existing penal case, in the court that entered the judgment.
data/rcap-all50/overlays/census-v1/hi/rcap-hi-custom-pleading--custom-pleading/participant-instructions.md:297:5. Serve a copy on the prosecuting attorney and complete the certificate of service on the motion, as Haw. R. Penal P. 49(a) and 49(c) require.
data/rcap-all50/overlays/census-v1/hi/rcap-hi-custom-pleading--custom-pleading/participant-instructions.md:299:7. Wait for the court to rule. Obtain a certified or signed copy of the order if it is granted.
data/rcap-all50/overlays/census-v1/hi/rcap-hi-custom-pleading--custom-pleading/participant-instructions.md:301:9. Enclose a copy of the signed court order, a copy of your valid government-issued photo ID, the payment the form specifies as a money order or cashier's check, and a self-addressed stamped envelope.
data/rcap-all50/overlays/census-v1/hi/rcap-hi-custom-pleading--custom-pleading/participant-instructions.md:309:- Every signature and every signature date, on the motion, on the declaration, on the certificate of service and on the stage-two application.
data/rcap-all50/overlays/census-v1/hi/rcap-hi-custom-pleading--custom-pleading/participant-instructions.md:323:The registry records these as self-help boundaries for these routes. Each one is a reason to stop and get help rather than to file this packet.
data/rcap-all50/overlays/census-v1/hi/rcap-hi-custom-pleading--custom-pleading/filing-instructions.md:7:**Where it goes.** The controlling record states: "Stage one: file a written motion in the existing penal case, in the court that entered the judgment. Stage two: submit the HCJDC 159(b) Expungement Application to the Hawaii Criminal Justice Data Center with a copy of the signed order attached."
data/rcap-all50/overlays/census-v1/hi/rcap-hi-custom-pleading--custom-pleading/filing-instructions.md:21:**Notice.** The controlling record states: "No statutory notice. Not one of the five provisions requires notice to the prosecuting attorney, to a victim, to the Attorney General, to the Data Center or to any agency. The notice that exists is the service every filed document receives."
data/rcap-all50/overlays/census-v1/hi/rcap-hi-custom-pleading--custom-pleading/filing-instructions.md:23:**Service, and the certificate of service.** The controlling record states: "Haw. R. Penal P. 49(a): all written submissions to the court shall be served upon each of the parties promptly after filing. The prosecuting attorney is a party to the underlying penal case and is served under that rule. Proof of service is required by Haw. R. Penal P. 49(c), so a certificate of service is part of the stage-one filing."
data/rcap-all50/overlays/census-v1/hi/rcap-hi-custom-pleading--custom-pleading/filing-instructions.md:25:The certificate of service is printed as part of the stage-one motion in this packet, on the motion's own last page. Complete it after you have served the copy, and not before.
data/rcap-all50/overlays/census-v1/hi/rcap-hi-custom-pleading--custom-pleading/filing-instructions.md:38:**What it costs.** The form's own face states: "The fee for first-time expungement is $35. Non-first-time expungements are $50. The fee includes a non-refundable $10 processing fee. A duplicate copy of an expungement certificate is $20.00." The form also states that payment must be made by money order or cashier's check issued in the United States, payable to "State of Hawaii", and that personal checks are not accepted.
data/rcap-all50/overlays/census-v1/hi/rcap-hi-custom-pleading--custom-pleading/filing-instructions.md:40:**Where it goes.** The form's own face prints the destination: Hawaii Criminal Justice Data Center, Attn: Expungement, 465 South King Street, Room 102, Honolulu, HI 96813. Send a self-addressed stamped envelope with it, as the form directs.
